    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Starships_of_the_Galaxy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy</a></i></p><table class=\"wikitable\">\n <tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <th>ATMOSPHERIC THRUSTERS</th>\n   <th>EMPLACEMENT POINTS</th>\n   <th>AVAILABILITY</th>\n   <th>SIZE RESTRICTION</th>\n   <th>COST</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>Standard</td>\n   <td>2</td>\n   <td>Common</td>\n   <td>Colossal or Smaller</td>\n   <td>2000 (Base)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>Advanced</td>\n   <td>5</td>\n   <td>Common</td>\n   <td>Gargantuan or Smaller</td>\n   <td>5000 (Base)</td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p>Atmospheric Thrusters increase a Starship's speed when the ship is flying in the atmosphere of a planet. Any Starship able to operate in an atmosphere has some engine system designed for air flight, normally a combination of repulsorlifts and ion engines. Atmospheric Thrusters are an augmentation of these base systems, designed to make the Starship more competitive with a dedicated <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Airspeeder\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Airspeeder\">Airspeeder</a>.</p><p>Standard Atmospheric Thrusters increase a Starship's maximum velocity and fly speed by 10%, while Advanced Atmospheric Thrusters increase these by 25% (rounded down to the nearest square of speed and 10 km/h). Thus, an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/X-Wing\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"X-Wing\">X-Wing</a> with Standard Atmospheric Thrusters has a maximum velocity of 1,150 km/h and a fly speed of 17 squares at <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Character_Scale\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Character Scale\">Character Scale</a>.</p><p>Atmospheric Thrusters have no effect on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Starship_Scale\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Starship Scale\">Starship Scale</a> movement.</p>",
